        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Ten minutes running under your own weight, a
            hand on the motor hood, and a look under the belt.</strong> Those three
            checks cover the failures that cost real money. A machine that cannot be
            demonstrated is not a bargain at any price, and neither is one that runs
            hot.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Confirm parts are still made for the model, budget for the van, and
            lubricate it before the first session using the
            <a href="/treadmill-belt-lubrication/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">lubrication guide</a>.
